# `at` is a slot held as a raw double. The read and the store of an element of a proven list take it as it is: the code turns it into an index once (truncate, back, compare); a fraction, NaN, what is too large or below zero go out of line.
# The slot stays a raw double only while every store into it is proven a number and nothing of the class escapes: so `seat` is handed a product, never an element of `keys` as it was read.
# RUN(READ): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# READ: [[key]]: number @Double = GetSlot {{*}}key="at"
# READ: = GetArrayElement {{*}}, [[key]] level=Expected
# RUN(STORE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# STORE: = PutArrayElement
# STORE-NOT: number @JSValue = Box
# Twenty-four keys (whole, minus zero, fractions, NaN, the infinities, the ends of the indices, of int32, of the whole doubles and of int64) on six kinds of list; added to zero, seated, and made by arithmetic on the field. Zero plus minus zero is zero: minus zero is seated.
